{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794238078,"nonce":"sKcz/X6VbiULCkWMfiWAxb7xLew=","title":"A normal Variable inside a value or source node of a face term evaluates to about half the magnitude","message":"With n = d.variable(face, normals=True), a Dirichlet value cross(g, n) in u.vector.cross(n) - cross(g, n), or the incident source cross(einc, n), gives a field about 0.49 times the exact one, uniformly. The same term with the constant vector (0,0,-1) in place of n gives the exact field (2.2 % discretisation error).\n\nReproduction: a homogeneous periodic box, the bottom face trace prescribed as cross(x, n), compare the field at a reference point with exp(i k (z + B)) x. Constant normal: 2.2 % error. Normal Variable: 0.49 times the field.","files":null}]}